{"availability":"available","full":"DanTruong/the-high-screen-jekyll","name":"the-high-screen-jekyll","description":"Static implementation of a sports and entertainment blog using Jekyll, Liquid, and GitHub Pages.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2020-12-16T20:10:29Z","updated":"2026-09-10T20:08:38Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dantruong.github.io/the-high-screen-jekyll/","topics":["bootstrap","github-pages","jekyll","react"],"demo":"https://dantruong.github.io/the-high-screen-jekyll/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.407Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.407Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.407Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.407Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An archive of the sports, pop culture, entertainment, and social commentary published by The High Screen from 2014–2015, rebuilt as a modern Jekyll project.","The High Screen began in 2014 as a collaborative sports and entertainment blog created by SUNY Oswego alumni Dan Truong, Joe Mags (@thatjoemags), and Moraima Capellán Pichardo (@MoraimaCP). The site was inspired by publications such as the former Grantland and gave its writers a place to continue producing features, columns, reviews, commentary, and other long-form work after college.","The original site ran on WordPress using traditional shared PHP hosting. After the publication became inactive, continuing to maintain paid hosting and an aging WordPress installation no longer made much sense. Rather than let the site and its articles disappear, the content was migrated to Jekyll so it could be preserved as a static archive and hosted through GitHub Pages with much less maintenance."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DanTruong/the-high-screen-jekyll/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ec008aebf028493760e694274f311d11a1b82d3665d6130b0374a525046799e","extractedAt